--- What NGA puts into your program ---

The licence above covers the tool. It does not cover what the tool puts into
a program it builds, which is yours to use without attribution: the files under
`lib/`, which carry their own licence (the Zero-Clause BSD licence, `lib/LICENSE`),
and every byte of 6502 code and every line of assembler text that NGA itself
writes into a build — the Transition routine, the Cell, the runtime of the C
subset, the text a `.ngc` Module or a generator compiles to. A program that
contains any of these is not a copy or a substantial portion of the Software
and is not subject to the licence above.

Third-party code the tool is built from, and the notices a binary of it must
carry, are listed in `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`.
